Spiridonas.wikitext:
{{ScythesOfTheEmperorPortal}}
'''Spiridonas''' was a [[Codicer]] of the [[Scythes of the Emperor]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1a}}

When the Chapter was forced to evacuate their [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|homeworld]], [[Sotha]], after it was attacked by the [[tyranid]]s of [[Hive Fleet Kraken]], Spiridonas was forced to use his [[Psyker|psychic abilities]] to pierce through the [[Shadow in the Warp]], acting as a [[Navigator]] for the fleet.  The resulting psychic strain was considerable, placing Spiridonas in a fugue state.{{Fn|1a}}

Eventually, Spiridonas was able to regain consciousness.  As he was the only surviving member of the Chapter's [[Librarius (Fortress-monastery)|Librarius]] to make it to their muster point in the [[Miral System]], [[Chapter Master]] [[Mansirius Thorcyra]] made him the Scythes' new [[Chief Librarian]].  It was initially the plan to send Spiridonas to one the Scythes' [[Ultramarines|cousin]] [[Successor Chapter|Chapters]] to complete his training, but Spiridonas received a vision that the tyranids had followed the Scythes from Sotha to [[Miral]].{{Fn|1b}}

At first, the Chapter Master did not heed the warning, as he regarded it as impossible for the tyranids to have followed them from Sotha to Miral so quickly at sublight speeds.{{Fn|1b}}  Nonetheless, the tyranids did indeed attack the Miral System, prompting Thorcyra to order the Chapter to make their stand at their outpost on the [[Giant's Coffin]].{{Fn|1c}}

Eventually, the tyranids overwhelmed every line of defence that the Scythes could establish and reached the bastion gates.  Spiridonas was killed after rescuing Bastion Commander [[Culmonios]] from a trio of [[Carnifex]]es.{{Fn|1d}}

