Steloc Aethon.wikitext:
{{UltramarinesPortal}}
[[Image:Calthcaptain.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] of the [[Ultramarines]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion's]] [[19th Company (Ultramarines Legion)|19th Company]]{{Fn|3}} and was a veteran of the [[Great Crusade]] when the [[Horus Heresy]] began.

==Biography==
A native of one of [[Calth]]'s noble families, he was brought up in the principle arcology of [[Gallica Subdelta]]. As his family's estates were mostly in the vast underground networks of Calth, he did not see the light of day for the first ten years of his life. During this time he became known as '''Aethon the White Spider''', due to his masterful knowledge of Calth's underground labyrinths.{{Fn|2}}

He eventually was pressed into the [[Ultramarines]], rising to the rank of [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] and aiding [[Roboute Guilliman]] himself in designing the world's defences.{{Fn|2}}

During the [[Great Crusade]], Aethon fought alongside the [[Word Bearers]] against [[Orks]], gaining a friendship with [[Kurtha Sedd]].{{Fn|2}} By the end of the Crusade, it was believed by many that Calth would become one of the ruling worlds of [[Ultramar]] and that it would receive its own [[Tetrarch of Ultramar|Tetrarch]]; Aethon was among the candidates being considered for the position.{{Fn|3}}

When the Word Bearers betrayed his Legion, he took part in the [[Battle for Calth]] and later became a [[Praetor (Rank)|Praetor]]. During the battle he led the Ultramarines' forces beneath Calth's surface against the Word Bearers who still infested it, in what became known as the '''Underground War'''.{{Fn|1}}

Unfortunately, Aethon's rage at his friend's betrayal would be his undoing. When his Company came into contact with Kurtha Sedd's warband, he fought his old battle brother hand to hand, but was ultimately slain. His death would be the catalyst for Kurtha Sedd unleashing a wave of [[Neverborn]] from the chasm his body was sent into. Fortunately for his Company, reinforcements from the Ultramarines would come, dissipating  forcing Sedd to retreat. {{Fn|4}}

==Wargear==
*''[[Moricorpus]]'' — [[Combi-Meltagun]].{{Fn|1}}

