Stolas.wikitext:
{{BloodAngelsPortal}}
'''Stolas''' was an [[Epistolary]] of the [[Blood Angels]] [[Chapter]], serving with the [[4th Company (Blood Angels)|4th Company]].{{Fn|1}}

Stolas was part of a 4th Company task force led by [[Chief Librarian]] [[Mephiston]] sent to the [[Supplicium System]] in response to a distress call sent by [[General]] [[Spira]] of the [[Mordian Iron Guard]].  Arriving at [[Supplicium Secundus]], the Blood Angels found that almost the entire population of the planet, along with the Mordians, had been corrupted by a rage-plague that led to them slaughtering each other.{{Fn|1}}

The Space Marines then received another distress call, this time from the other inhabited planet of the [[system]], [[Supplicium Tertius]], revealing that the plague had spread there as well.  As they made their way to the other planet, they encountered the shadow of a lost Blood Angels [[Battle Barge]] known as the ''[[Eclipse of Hope]]''.  This [[warp]]-corrupted vessel was the source of the madness afflicting the system and the Blood Angels were forced to board it, as it was unaffected by their [[Strike Cruiser|Strike Cruiser's]] weapons.{{Fn|1}}

Mephiston himself led the boarding action, accompanied by Stolas along with [[Chaplain]] [[Dantalion (Blood Angels)|Dantalion]], [[Sanguinary Priest]] [[Albinus]], [[Techmarine]] [[Phenex]] and [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Gamigin]].  After determining that the source of the [[Chaos]] corruption on the ''Eclipse of Hope'' was located in the ship's [[Librarium]], the Marines made their way there, with Mephiston and Stolas entering alone to confront the warp-taint.  While attempting to exorcise the Librarium, Stolas gave in to the temptation of infinite knowledge offered by the Chaos powers at work and was killed by Mephiston.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Eclipse of Hope (Short Story)]]

