{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Szabo''' was a [[Major]] of the [[Brevian Centennials]] active during the [[Sabbat Worlds Crusade]].{{Fn|1a}}


==Biography==
Prior to the Sabbat Crusade, Szabo participated in the winter-wars on [[Aex Eleven]].{{Fn|1b}}

Szabo took part in the [[Hagia]] campaign, commanding Brevian forces assigned to the capture of Hagia's capital, the [[Holy Doctrinopolis]], which had been overrun by the [[Infardi]] under [[Pater (Chaos)|Pater]] [[Sin]].{{Fn|1a}} Although the Imperials were making good headway in taking the city, the impatience of [[Lord General]] [[Lugo]] resulted in him ordering the Imperial forces to forego the infantry-based approach advocated by [[Colonel-Commissar]] [[Ibram Gaunt]] in favour of an armoured assault by the [[Eighth Pardus Armoured]].{{Fn|1a}}{{Fn|1b}} Following this attack, Szabo and the Brevians moved to secure the Citadel.{{Fn|1b}}

Unfortunately for the Imperials, Pater Sin had prepared a ritual trap at the Citadel, which was triggered by the Brevians' approach.{{Fn|1b}} The ritual destroyed the Citadel, killing Szabo and the rest of the deployed Brevians.{{Fn|1b}}{{Fn|1c}}

