'''Illuminor Szeras''' is a famed [[Necron]] [[Cryptek]] and overseer of the [[Zantragora Conclave]] who specializes in bioscience.{{Fn|11}}{{Fn|4b}}

=== History ===
While the [[C'tan]] might have provided the knowledge for the [[biotransference]], it was Szeras who made it a reality millions of years ago as a [[Necrontyr]]. Even then, he saw it as the first step on the path to ultimate evolution into beings of pure energy.{{Fn|4a}}{{Fn|11}} He has since established himself on the [[Tomb World]] of [[Zantragora]]{{Fn|4a}} as head of the [[Zantragora Conclave]] of Crypteks which seek to unravel the mysteries of life.{{Fn|4b}}

Szeras constantly labors to unravel the mysteries of life, for he fears that he would be a poor god without the secrets of life at his fingertips. But certain concepts displayed in organic lifeforms escape, which frustrates his cold logical mindset. Refusing to abandon his quest, he requires a constant flow of living subjects for brutal experimentation and agonizing testing in his scientific quests.  He acquires experimental subjects by raiding the worlds of the younger races.{{Fn|2}} Though he is obsessed with the secrets of life, his aptitude for augmenting the weaponry and mechanical bodies of other Necrons is peerless. As a result his talents are in high demand by other [[Necron Overlord]]s.{{Fn|1}} Such is the demand for Szeras that he can name his own price - invariably a harvesting raid of a  world of his choosing. The unfortunate victims that fall into Szeras' clutches can look forward only to a brief pain-filled existence as they are experimented on his the laboratories beneath Zantragora. Above all, he covets the [[Eldar]] for study and experimentation.{{Fn|4a}} He has also shown bafflement at the faith-based abilities of the [[Sisters of Battle]], which can result in supernatural abilities that not even Szeras' science can explain.{{Fn|7}}

It is known that Szeras waited on [[Nectavus VI]] for the day when the Warp would break free and he would behold the death of an entire planet. As around him erupts a cataclysmic event, Illuminor Szeras calls upon his lurking armies and begins to pursue his own inscrutable goals. The obsession of Szeras with the nature of biological life has led him to create new forms of repair on his own necron soldiers, and his experiments have, in many cases, improved the effectiveness of the mechanical bodies of his servants.{{Fn|3}}

Eventually Szeras was able to improve his own form. The dissection of [[Vuzsalen Arachtoid]] compound eyes unlocked an improved array for targeting optics, and the molecular disassembling of [[Ambull]] hide led to more efficient armor.{{Fn|7a}} He also wields devastating offensive technologies, using atomic manipulators to decompose his foes in the midst of battle or unleashing empyrean overloaders to destroy the minds of [[Psyker]]s.{{Fn|8}}

Upon the return of the [[Silent King]] [[Szarekh]], Szeras has joined him on the campaign to reverse [[Biotransference]]. Szarekh was able to convince Szeras that reversing the process he himself set into motion would give him the ultimate revelations he has been searching for.{{Fn|8}} 

Since the formation of the [[Great Rift]], Szeras worked with the [[Silent King]] [[Szarekh]] and the [[Nihilakh Dynasty]] to erect the [[Pariah Nexus]] in the [[Nephilim Sector]]. Thousands within the Pariah Nexus have since been captured and brought to Szeras' laboratories for experimentation.{{Fn|8}} During the [[War in the Pariah Nexus]] he viewed the [[Imperial]] invaders as little more than vermin and hoped to study the effect the Nexus would have on them. However his trap soon turned into a series of frustrations for the Cryptek due to the presence of [[Ephrael Stern]], whose faith-based power the Necrons had little counter for. During the battle on in the [[Tredica System]], [[Inquisitor]] [[Draxus]] unleashed a captive [[C'tan Shard]] held at the heart of a [[Pylon]] complex. Szeras immediately lost interest in the humans upon this development and became desperate to contain the raging Star God.{{Fn|7}} 

Szaeras later appeared once again in the court of the Silent King during the later stages of the [[War in the Pariah Nexus]], working alongside the [[Technomandrites]] to complete the Pariah Nexus project in the face of Imperial, [[Chaos]], and [[Imotekh]]'s attacks.{{Fn|9}}

=== Wargear ===
Szeras wields an [[Eldritch Lance]]. He has also equipped himself with an [[Empyric Overcharger]] that can nullify psychic abilities.{{Fn|7}}

