T'sathis Vhorr.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[Exalted Sorcerer]] of the [[Cult of Time]] of the [[Thousand Sons]].{{Fn|1}}

==Overview==
[[file:VhorrArt.jpg|thumb|right|200px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1}}]]
Through many [[Daemonic]] pacts and arcane research, {{PAGENAME}} has gained partial control over the streams of time itself. He has further mastered the ability of loosening time's grip upon him and most of his followers. His Thrallband, the [[Blades of Sinister]], are able to vanish from the timeline of realspace at will, only to reappear at times where they could not possibly do so normally. They have used this to ambush foes that sought to ambush them and even tricked their enemies into choosing contradictory paths at precisely the same fixed moment in time, shattering them across infinite time streams through weaponized impossibility.{{Fn|1}}

However, constantly slipping through time has eroded {{PAGENAME}}'s own place in it. Though his followers see this as a blessing of [[Tzeentch]], the Sorcerer is constantly surrounded by blurred simulations of himself, each acting slightly before or after him and subtly choosing different paths. This has made it incredibly difficult to strike him in battle, with his foes often striking these temporal phantoms instead. However, this ability is a double-edged sword, for should it become too pronounced Vhorr will lose his place in the time-stream altogether. To counteract this, he has fashioned a staff that acts as a temporal anchor which if destroyed may see him shattered across space and time.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Thousand Sons (9th Edition)]], pg. 22
