Tagore.wikitext:
{{WorldEatersPortal}}

{{PAGENAME}} was a [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] in the [[World Eaters]]' 15th Company.{{fn|1a}}

==Biography==
{{Spoiler|source=The Outcast Dead (Novel)}}
Tagore was part of the XII Legio when it was still called the '''War Hounds''', and was outfitted with the [[Butcher's Nails]].{{fn|1c}}

He was one of the Astartes assigned to the [[Crusader Host]], and had not been with his Legion for over a century{{fn|1c}}, when the [[Horus Heresy]] broke out. At that point, [[Rogal Dorn]] ordered the Host be captured, and [[Yasu Nagasena]] led a force of 3,000 men to that aim, 359 of whom Tagore killed.{{fn|1b}}

When [[Atharva]] enacted his plan to break himself and his fellow Astartes out of [[Khangba Marwu]], Tagore brutally killed Uttam of the [[Legio Custodes]].{{fn|1b}} Adamantly loyal to [[Angron]], he was one of the [[Outcast Dead]] bent on going back to their respective Legions although he was equally ready to fight his [[Primarch]] to the death should he prove a traitor{{fn|1c}}, and was a fierce proponent of the [[Imperial Truth]].{{fn|1d}}

When the Palace's hunters assaulted the Temple of Woe where the Outcast Dead had cremated their fallen comrades, Tagore dueled Nagasena. The hunter grievously wounded him but Tagore nearly broke his opponent's neck, only to be brought down by a plasma bolt fired by [[Maxim Golovka]].{{fn|1e}}

