Tamino Degarlos Vermelk Helmawr.wikitext:
{{NecromundaPortal}}
'''Tamino Degarlos Vermelk Helmawr'''{{Fn|1}} (born '''971.[[M41]]''') is the 14th recognized son of [[Gerontius Helmawr]], the [[Imperial Commander|137th Lord]] of [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]].{{Fn|2d}}

==History==
Unlike his siblings, Tamino never desired to succeed his father and become the [[Hive World]]'s next [[Imperial Commander|ruler]]. He instead preferred to pursue more visceral activities, that allowed Tamino to get his hands dirty. In his mind, what was the point of [[House Helmawr]]'s wealth and the training he underwent as one of Lord [[Gerontius Helmawr|Helmawr]]'s recognized children, if he could not do so? Despite this, Tamino's sister [[Haera Helmawr]] tried to kill him on multiple occasions, in her quest to succeed their Father. While these attempts failed and led to Tamino not liking his sister, he respected the ambition that Haera had.{{Fn|1}}

In [[M42]], the [[Great Rift]]'s [[Noctis Aeterna]] struck the [[Hive World]] and in the mayhem that followed, an [[Assassin]]'s attack left [[Gerontius Helmawr|Gerontius]] in a [[Stasis Casket]]. With their Father now unable to rule [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]], a power struggle broke out between Gerontius' heirs to replace him as its [[Imperial Commander]].{{Fn|2a}} [[Lady Credo]], though, used the opportunity to launch a [[Credo Rebellion|world-wide rebellion]] to end [[House Helmawr]]'s rule of the Hive World.{{Fn|2b}}

In the mayhem that followed, many of Gerontius' heirs were killed by various forces. However, his daughter [[Haera Helmawr]] became the [[Imperial House]]'s de facto ruler{{Fn|2d}} after she asked her surviving siblings to attend a family meeting and then killed them all.{{Fn|2c}} Tamino and six other heirs were not there though, and they are now likely hiding to avoid their cruel sister's grasp.{{Fn|2d}} Afterwards though, [[Lady Credo]] freed her master [[Ozostium Aranthus]], who was revealed to be the leader behind the rebellion and this led Haera to begin to lose her grip on Necromunda. Soon Ozostium's forces swept across the Hive World and a desperate Haera attempted to reach the [[Dust Wall]], in order to gather its forces that watched over [[Hive Secundus]] to her side. During this time, Tamino had already made his way to Secundus and was exploring its ruins, while wearing a [[Malcadon Spyrer]] suit. As he did so, Tamino learned many of the secrets the Hive contained, including information that had been sealed away by his [[Gerontius Helmawr|Father]] or was no longer available anywhere else on Necromunda.{{Fn|1}} 

[[Haera Helmawr|Haera]] meanwhile, failed to reach the [[Dust Wall]], after her party was hunted down by [[Ash Waste Nomad]]s commanded by the [[Spirit Speaker]] [[Asun'ghar]]. The pursuit finally ended in the lost underground hold of the [[Ironhead Squat Prospector]] clan [[Jardlan]] and only Haera is known to have escaped. However she was left badly wounded by Asun'ghar and collapsed after reaching the underground passage that led to the ruins of [[Hive Secundus]]. She was later found by Tamino, who briefly considered leaving his Sister to be killed by the things that hunted the tunnels there. In the end though, Tamino knew he was not like his siblings and chose to save Haera by injecting her with [[Stimm]]s. Once healed, Haera told Tamino that she needed to reach the Dust Wall in order to prevent [[Ozostium Aranthus]] from overthrowing [[House Helmawr]]'s [[Imperial Commander|rule]] of [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]]. Tamino informed her, however, that the Dust Wall had been lost to Ozostium's forces but that his exploration of Hive Secundus' ruins had allowed him to learn much about [[House Aranthus]]. He also found something that would kill the god-like Ozostium and in doing so, finally bring the [[Credo Rebellion|rebellion]] to an end. Tamino then led Haera into Hive Secundus to show her the power he had discovered. At that time, it is believed the two were the only recognized children of Lord [[Gerontius Helmawr]], that were still alive.{{Fn|1}}

