Tanthius (Primaris Captain).wikitext:
{{FleshTearersPortal}}
'''Tanthius''' is the [[Primaris Captain]] of the [[Flesh Tearers]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Space Marine Company|4th Company]].{{Fn|1a}}

==Biography==
He is a veteran of the [[Indomitus Crusade]] and was among the [[Blood Angels]] [[Primaris Space Marines|Primaris]] [[Greyshields]] that were sent to replenish the [[Flesh Tearers]]' ranks, after the [[Devastation of Baal]]. However, while they were welcomed into the [[Chapter]], the Primaris faced harsh remarks and judgement from high ranking [[Firstborn]] Flesh Tearers like [[High Chaplain]] [[Appollus]], [[Chapter Champion]] [[Harahel]], and even at times from their [[Chapter Master]] [[Gabriel Seth]] as well. This was due to their connection to the hated [[Lord Commander]] [[Guilliman]] and because the Firstborn viewed the Primaris as newborns, who were not true born sons of the Chapter's founder [[Amit]]. Despite this attitude, though, Seth made full use of the Primaris' strength, as the Flesh Tearers took part in the [[Blood Angels]]' [[Angel's Halo]] campaign.{{Fn|1a}} 

Sometime later, however, Tanthius and his [[Space Marine Company|Company]] were chosen by Chapter Master Seth to return to the [[Flesh Tearers]]' [[Adeptus Astartes Homeworld|Homeworld]] [[Cretacia]]. At that point, due to the [[Warp]], it had been twenty years since the [[Chapter]] had departed their world, to take part in the [[Devastation of Baal]]. They had not received any contact from Cretacia during that time and while a detachment of Flesh Tearers had been left behind to defend it, Seth had decided to find out its fate. Tanthius, however, objected to leaving the [[Angel's Halo]] campaign before it was done and tried to convince the Chapter Master that Cretacia was likely fine. In his view, the world would have called out for aid if it was in danger and his Company should continue to fight beside the rest of the Chapter. [[High Chaplain]] [[Appollus]] took issue with Tanthius's refusal to follow orders and the two nearly came to blows, before Seth had the [[Chapter Champion]] [[Harahel]] break them apart. The Chapter Master then reaffirmed his orders and charged Tanthius with both securing their Homeworld and also the relics that were stored there.{{Fn|1a}} 

Tanthius was ultimately unable to return to Cretacia, being killed by a [[Genestealer Cult]] [[Clamavus]] aboard the [[Lunar Class Cruiser]] ''[[Herald of Virtue]]'' close to the [[Corythos System]]. Dumah was forced to lead the rest of the expedition himself.{{Fn|1b}}

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Wrath of the Lost (Novel)]]
**{{Endn|1a}}: Chapter 1
**{{Endn|1b}}: Chapters 5-6

