Tanthius (Terminator Sergeant).wikitext:
{{BloodRavensPortal}}
'''Tanthius''' is a [[Terminator Sergeant]] in the [[Blood Ravens]] [[3rd Company (Blood Ravens)|Third Company]].{{Fn|1a}}
==History==
He fought in the [[Tartarus]] Campaign when the Company came to the aid of the beleaguered planet as it was being invaded by [[Ork]]s.  Tanthius was tasked with taking ninth squadron and shoring up the southern flank in the defense of Magna Bonum.{{Fn|1}}  As events unfolded, Tanthius would aid his [[Space Marine Company|Company]] in fighting not only the Orks, but also the [[Eldar]] of [[Craftworld]] [[Biel-tan]] and the [[Alpha Legion]] as well, when the [[Traitor Marines|traitors]] began their plot to unlock the [[Daemon]]ic [[Maledictum]].{{Fn|2}}  Tanthius fought valiantly through all of [[Mankind|Mankind's]] enemies that ravaged the planet and participated in the final battle against the Alpha Legion, which saw the [[Daemon Prince|ascended]] [[Sindri Myr]] defeated.  Afterwards, when the Blood Ravens departed Tartarus, Tanthius was presented with a master-crafted [[Thunder Hammer]] and [[Storm Shield]] that [[Arms of Tanthius|bear his name]] in honour of his ceaseless fight against the Chapter's enemies.{{Fn|3}}
==Trivia==
{{trivia}}
==={{Endn|Conflicting sources}}===
In the first [[Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War|Dawn of War]], Tanthius was found dead by the [[Blood Ravens]] after their victory over [[Warboss]] [[Orkamungus]], in the completion cutscene for the campaign mission ''Destroy the Xenos'', having been killed by the [[Alpha Legion]] during their battle with the [[Orks]]{{Fn|2}}. In the [[Warhammer 40,000: Dawn of War II|Dawn of War II]] wargear selection screen for the [[Arms of Tanthius]], however, he is reported to have survived the campaign on [[Tartarus]].{{Fn|3}}

