Tarkus.wikitext:
{{BloodRavensPortal}}
[[Image:Tarkus.jpg|thumb|right|Sergeant Tarkus]]
{{otheruses|USE=Blood Ravens Sergeant|OTHERUSE=other uses of the term|OTHERPAGE=Tarkus (disambiguation)}}
'''Tarkus''' is a [[Tactical Squad]] [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] in the [[Blood Ravens]] [[4th Company (Blood Ravens)|4th Company]]. He is a veteran with over 150 years of experience in warfare, and is an expert tactician as well as a rock-solid second-in-command. Amongst his tactical marines, Tarkus is renowned for his confidence and steely demeanour in battle. Tarkus's native world is [[Calderis]].{{Cite This}}

==Biography==
Tarkus was awarded [[Terminator Honours]] for his involvement in the assault on the [[Necron]] Catacombs of [[Kronus]], where he and his squad repelled waves after waves of Necron forces to buy [[Space Marine Captain|Captain]] [[Davian Thule]] time to plant the bomb that would end the Necron threat to the planet.{{Cite This}}

During the [[First Aurelian Crusade]], Tarkus once again served alongside Captain Thule in his defence of [[Subsector Aurelia]].{{Fn|1}}

===The Penitent===
Tarkus was once convinced by an [[Eldar Ranger]] to lead his squad straight into an ambush. The Ranger had approached him under the guise of a truce and had proposed they temporarily work together against their common enemy, the Orks.{{Cite This}}

Tarkus was the sole survivor of the ambush and has never forgiven himself for the deaths of his men. The fact that the deceitful Eldar Ranger escaped the fight also weighs upon him and kindles a deep hatred for the Eldar that has not lessened with time.{{Cite This}}

==Equipment==
Tarkus wields a Standard Issue .998 Godwyn pattern [[Bolter]] in combat. He is also able to wield a MK IIIa "Heretic" Pattern [[Flamer]], or a [[Plasma Gun]].{{Fn|1}} During the [[Second Aurelian Crusade]] he was also able to wield a [[Meltagun]].{{Fn|2}}

If Tarkus gains the Melee Aptitude trait he may equip a [[Bolt Pistol]] and [[Chainsword]]. He can later wield a [[Power Sword]] if he gains the Power Sword Aptitude trait.{{Fn|1}}

==Trivia==
{{Trivia}}
===Conflicting sources===
In [[Dawn of War II (Novel)|the novelization]] of [[Dawn of War 2]], Tarkus is last seen leading his squad on a boarding mission aboard the last [[Tyranid]] [[Hive Ship]] in orbit over [[Meridian]]. He and his men are outnumbered, and the clear implication is that all are killed by the Tyranids, though not before completing their mission and fatally wounding the ship.{{Fn|3}}

However, in the game series, there is no boarding mission aboard a Hive Ship{{Fn|1}}, and Tarkus survives the Tyranid attack and continues to serve alongside [[Aramus]] in the campaign against the [[Black Legion]].{{Fn|2}}

