Ted Torvin.wikitext:
{{AstraMilitarumPortal}}
'''Ted Torvin''' is a [[Guardsman]] in the newly created [[Skadi Second Infantry]] [[Regiment]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
Born into a wealthy [[Skadi (Hive World)|Skadi]] family, Torvin was close to marrying his fiance, [[Melina]], when he was among those on his [[Hive]] sub-sector to be tithed to the [[Regiment]]. At first, Torvin paniced and thought about deserting and escaping with Melina into the [[Underhive|lower levels]] of his Hive. He ultimately decided not to, however, as he loved Melina too much to have her live that kind of life. The fact that deserters on Skadi are shot on sight also added to Torvin's decision to show up for his tithing. As the [[Skadi Second Infantry]] left for their basic training on the [[Hive World]]'s moon, '''Edda''', Torvin knew it was likely that he would never see Melina again. He kept a [[Pict]] of her with him at all times and it was the one personal item he would take from home. 80 days later, the Regiment was shipped off to [[Gondwa VI]], where they would protect the world from an [[Ork]] invasion. After they arrived and prepared to face the [[Xenos]], Torvin was not only convinced that he would not see Melina again, but that he would also not survive his first battle either.{{Fn|1}}

However, Torvin found himself the only survivor of the [[Regiment]], when the [[Orks]] overwhelmed '''Outpost Four''' which the [[Skadi Second Infantry|Second Infantry]] had been defending. Afterwards, he was sent to join the newly arrived [[Catachan 57th Jungle Fighters]]. However Torvin was not welcomed by [[Colonel]] [[Haskell Aldalon]] and the 57th, who considered him to be a barely trained [[Guardsman]]. Worse still, they assumed Torvin's survival against the Orks' attack, was only due to his cowardice. This has led him to become at risk from both the 57th and the Orks, as the Catachan Regiment now seeks to reclaim the lost Outpost Four. This will come at a cost, however, since the invading [[Xenos]] have the [[Imperium]] on the defensive. Now as the 57th advance into Ork held territory, Torvin must undergo a trial by fire in order to earn his new Regiment's respect.{{Fn|2}}

==Sources==
