Teknoth.wikitext:
{{NecronsPortal}}
'''Teknoth the Dread''' is a [[Necron]] [[Royal Warden]], who serves a great [[Phaeron]] of the [[Szarekhan Dynasty]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
He is a renowned battle-champion, who has felled countless foes and constantly brags about his accomplishments. This led Teknoth to come to the notice of the [[Nihilakh Dynasty]] [[Necron Overlord|Overlord]] [[Trazyn the Infinite]] in [[M42]], who decided to abduct the [[Royal Warden]] to fight in his arena. This was partly done to see if the [[Royal Warden]] lived up to his bragging and to also annoy the arrogant Teknoth. He was not the only warrior brought to the arena, which is located within the Overlord's hidden '''Sanctum''' and connected to the [[Tomb World]] [[Solemnace]], via [[Reality-Tether]]s. Facing the Warden was the [[Blood Angel]] [[Rafelo]], the [[Ultramarine]] [[Markus Castus]] and the [[Death Guard]] [[Refulgus Grue]], who were all brought there to fight for Trazyn's amusement. The Overlord promised, however, that he would free the last fighter who remained standing. For his part, Teknoth is furious about his imprisonment and is determined to prove his superiority to the other warriors, before he escapes and exacts his punishment upon Trazyn. However unbeknownst to the Warden and the other warriors, the Overlord has no intention of freeing the arena winner. Instead the victor will have the honor of taking a place of pride within Trazyn's latest exhibit on Solemnace.{{Fn|1a}} 

