The Lady of the Voids.wikitext:
{{SlaaneshPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a name given by the [[Imperium]] to an unknown breed of [[Slaanesh]] [[Daemon]]s that are often part of the vile host that trails its voidships as they travel established [[Warp–route]]s.{{Fn|1a}}

==Overview==
[[Image:The Lady of The Voids.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}{{Fn|1a}}]]
However, unlike her lesser brethren who can merely follow the ship ineffectually, a Lady can prey upon a moment of weakness from a [[Navigator]] or [[Astropath]] in order to [[Daemonic Possession|possess]] them and pass through their vessel's [[Geller field]]. The Lady then manifests aboard the vessel by causing their possessed victim's body to burst apart; the sight of the Lady draped in the torn flesh and entrails of their former crewmember, combined with her nightmarish physical appearance is enough to break the weak of will of anyone aboard the vessel. The Daemon appears as a nightmarish merging of several female bodies about a vertical axis—faces, arms, and mouths facing in different directions; while her torso is a hideous mix of woman, crab, and bloated toad, whilst half of her arms end in spiny pincers.{{Fn|1a}}

The most dangerous thing about the Lady, however, is her constant siren call which can make anyone hearing it go mad. As soon as she appears the Lady's many voices scream and moan this dreadful Warp–song, which enraptures all who hear it. To them, the Lady is a beauty to burn the soul and their sanity flees as the Warp–song melts their mind, and soon causes a foaming madness to take hold of the afflicted. Some crewmen begin mutilating themselves; others turn to destroy tech–devices, murder one other, or struggle to open the seal–gates and let in the void. Eventually though they all fall under the Daemon's will and the Lady gleefully sweeps through the stricken vessel at the head of a growing horde of the insane; set upon multiplying the suffering of her puppets in an orgy of destruction and death.{{Fn|1a}}

Though their doom is almost certain, there are some measures the crew of a stricken vessel can do to save themselves: of vital importance of course is to make sure they can not hear the Lady's siren song. Plugging their ears, constantly yelling the [[Emperor]]'s praises, or even sealing themselves within an insulated area can help save them from the Daemon's voice. The most direct way, however, is to face the Lady in battle and send her screaming back into the [[Warp]]. Though they would have to face a maddened horde composed of their fellow crewmen to do so, ending the Lady's song would save their vessel and free those who fell under the Daemon's power.{{Fn|1b}}

