The Visarch.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
[[Image:VisarchArt.jpg|thumb|right|220px|{{PAGENAME}}]]
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is an [[Eldar]] known as the '''Sword of Ynnead''' and serves the newly awakened [[Eldar God]] [[Ynnead|of the Dead]].{{Fn|1}}

==History==
The Visarch was originally a [[Biel-tan]] [[Dire Avenger]] [[Exarch]] of the [[Silvered Blade Shrine]], known as '''Laarian Starspeaker''' and had considerable standing with his [[Craftworld]]{{Fn|5}}. He met [[Yvraine]] when she was just a mere [[Aspect Warrior]], teaching her much of swordsmanship. Laarian grew close to his student and developed strong feelings for her. He was much saddened when Yvraine left his shrine and chose to instead become a Witch and then Outcast. When she joined the murderers of [[Commorragh]], his spirit broke and his feelings for Yvraine diverted the course of his path. In a nigh-unprecedented decision, Laarian left his Shrine and decided to follow Yvraine.{{Fn|4a}}

The Visarch reappeared in [[Commorragh]] at the side of the newly awakened Emissary of [[Ynnead]], [[Yvraine]]. During this time, he posed as an [[Incubus]] in the [[Shrine of the Coiled Blade]]. As an Incubus he became infamous, known as the '''Scarlet Incubi'''. He later struck down the Shrine's Klaivex and took his position by right of conquest.{{Fn|4a}} He was later instrumental in Yvraine's escape from the Dark City and the formation of the [[Ynarri]]. He now acts as the guardian of Yvraine and has fought alongside her on her expeditions to resurrect [[Ynnead]].{{Fn|2}} The Visarch later accompanied Yvraine to [[Kalisus]] where they brought the survivors of the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]] to [[Macragge]]. The Visarch fought alongside Imperial forces in the subsequent [[Ultramar Campaign]].{{Fn|3}} The Visarch continues to serve Yvraine as one of her chief protectors, and during the [[Battle of Iathglas]] was nearly killed by [[Shalaxi Helbane]]. His apparent death was enough to summon [[Yncarne]], but after the battle Yvraine was able to regenerate his broken form.{{Fn|4b}}

The Visarch accompanied Yvraine and the Ynnari in the search for the last [[Cronesword]], believed to be a portal found only on the lost [[Craftworld]] of [[Zaisuthra]]. During the journey, the [[Harlequins]] of the [[Masque of the Midnight Sorrow]] mentally tested each of the core leaders of the Ynnari, and only the Visarch was found wanting. [[Shadowseer]] [[Laedellin Starshone]] said that the Visarch would betray Yvraine one day.{{Fn|6a}} Later during the battle against [[Genestealer]]-corrupted Eldar on Zaisuthra, it is the Visarch that brings Yvraine back from being overcome by the wrath of [[Ynnead]].{{Fn|6b}} However later as they battle the [[Warshard]] in the tomb of [[Eldanesh]], it is the Visarch who is overcome by the murderous rage of [[Khaine]], and this time it leads to Yvraine willingly letting herself be struck down in order to manifest [[Yncarne]].{{Fn|6c}} Yvraine is resurrected by Yncarne, and after the battle she absolves the Visarch for earlier his actions.{{Fn|6d}} 

The Visarch fought alongside Yvraine and the Ynnari once more on [[Agarimethea]].{{Fn|7}}

==Wargear==
In battle, the Visarch wields the [[Crone Sword]] [[Asu-Var]] and wears ancient armour of the [[Bel-Anshoc]] style.{{Fn|5}}

