Thelugh Poxmaw.wikitext:
{{DeathGuardPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Death Guard]] [[Chaos Lord]] who serves in the [[Apostles of Contagion]] Warband and took part in the [[Thirteenth Black Crusade]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
After the [[Great Rift]]'s creation during the Crusade, the forces of [[Nurgle]] seized three [[Imperial]] [[system]]s that became the [[Scourge Stars]]; these became used as a staging ground to invade [[Ultramar]]. As the [[Daemon Primarch]] [[Mortarion]] began to muster the [[Death Guard]]'s forces for the [[Plague Wars|invasion]], several Warbands attacked nearby Imperial worlds to prevent them from stopping the Daemon Primarch's plans. The Apostles of Contagion were one of those Warbands and Poxmaw led his forces in an invasion of the world [[Daxar]].{{Fn|1}}

They met resistance in the form of a [[Astra Militarum]] strike force, built around the [[Cadian Shock Troopers|56th Cadian heavy infantry]]. Despite the [[Guardsmen]]s efforts, the Apostles drove them back across the world's desert. However, at the desert's end was a passage known as '''Tarran's Pass''', which the Guardsmen fortified and used to repel every attempt the Apostles made to destroy them. Conscious that the Guardsmen were planning a counterattack that could destroy the now depleted Apostles' forces, Poxmaw ordered his [[Sorcerer]]s to summon several hundred [[Beasts of Nurgle]]. Once the summoning was complete, Poxmaw sent the [[Daemon]]s towards the Guardsmen and, though dozens of the beasts were destroyed, the Daemons broke through their defences. As the Beasts of Nurgle then began rampaging within the Guardsmen's forces, Poxmaw led what remained of the Apostles to destroy them and end the threat Daxar posed to the Scourge Stars.{{Fn|1}}

==Sources==
