Thirianna.wikitext:
{{EldarPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Seer]] of [[Craftworld]] [[Alaitoc]].{{Fn|1a}}

===Biography===
[[Image:SeerNovelCover.jpg|thumb|right|250px|{{PAGENAME}} as a [[Farseer]]{{Fn|1h}}]]
As a [[Dire Avenger]] [[Aspect Warrior]], {{PAGENAME}} executed a [[Human]] woman and her children during a mission after their commanding [[Farseer]] ordered the world tainted by [[Chaos]].{{Fn|1a}} Shaken by the experience, she left the [[Path of the Warrior]] and walked the [[Path of the Poet]], where she reunited with her childhood friends [[Korlandril]] and [[Aradryan]]. After Aradryan criticized Korlandril's new sculpture and both Korlandril Aradryan makes unrequited romantic overtures to {{PAGENAME}}, their friendship fractured. Korlandril entered the [[Striking Scorpion]]s, Aradryan became an [[Eldar Ranger]] on the [[Path of the Outcast]], and {{PAGENAME}} entered the [[Path of the Seer]].{{Fn|1b}}

Training under the [[Farseer]] [[Kelamith]], {{PAGENAME}} learned to access Alaitoc's [[Infinity Circuit]] and divine the skein of fate.{{Fn|1c}} Aradryan eventually returned to Alaitoc, bringing word of an [[Ork]] attack on the [[Exodite World]] pf [[Eileniliesh]]. Alaitoc sent aid, and {{PAGENAME}} reunited with both Aradryan and Korlandril. Troubled by the paths they have taken, she nonetheless was able to use her abilities to guide the Eldar forces in battle and emerge victorious over the Orks.{{Fn|1d}} 

Frustrated by her limitations, {{PAGENAME}} attempted to explore the [[Webway]] alone despite warnings to not attempt it by her instructors. Coming across a [[Dark Eldar]] pirate outpost, her fear attracted [[Daemon]]s of [[Slaanesh]]. She was rescued at the last moment by Kelamith. Afterwards, {{PAGENAME}} was told to progress further she must have a personal rune fashioned by her estranged father, the [[Bonesinger]] [[Yrlandriar]]. After looking into the past and understanding her father's grief at the loss of their mother, she was able to reconcile with her father and he agreed to craft her rune.{{Fn|1e}}

While practicing with her increased powers, {{PAGENAME}} witnessed a horrifying vision where Alaitoc was destroyed by an [[Imperial]] attack. She brought her vision before the [[Seer Council]] but it was dismissed as she was just a novice. {{PAGENAME}} was then able to manipulate Korlandril, now part of the psyche of the [[Exarch]] [[Morlaniath]], into bringing the vision to the [[Autarch]] [[Arhathain]], who was able to finally get Alaitoc to take it seriously.{{Fn|1f}}

Thanks to her actions, Alaitoc was able to survive the [[Siege of Alaitoc|Imperial invasion]] though she was briefly overcome by a [[Space Marine]] [[Librarian]], who hacked into her mind to divine the Eldar troop movements.{{Fn|1g}}

