Thirteenth Curse.wikitext:
{{BlackLegionPortal}}
The '''Thirteenth Curse''' is the name given by the [[Imperium]], to an unknown coven of five powerful [[The Assignment|alpha-level]] [[Black Legion]] [[Sorcerers]]. They were first encountered by the Imperium during the [[Nachmund Rift War]]'s invasion of the [[Sanctus Wall]] world [[Catagyl]], which is currently on-going.{{Fn|1}} 
==History==
Each of the unknown [[Sorcerers]]' [[psychic]] might has been heavily augmented and is now nearly at apocalyptic levels. The [[Imperium]] does not know how this occurred though, various theories have been stated. This includes the Thirteenth Curse's proximity to the [[Great Rift]], some unknown property of [[Catagyl]] or because of its population's lack of [[Imperial Cult|faith]], as several [[Priests]] have claimed. Regardless of how it has occurred, the Thirteenth Curse's might has allowed them to turn every battle they join into a devastating defeat for the Imperium's forces. However the coven now numbers four Sorcerers, after the '''Fiend''' was slain by members of the [[Sisters of Silence]].{{Fn|1}}
==Known Members== 
*The '''Eye''' - Turned two hundred [[Guardsmen]] inside out with a single gesture, during the [[Imperium]]'s retreat from '''Casmis'''.{{Fn|1}}
*The '''Fiend''' - Destroyed several [[Imperial]] armies by himself, before being slain by the [[Sisters of Silence]]. His powers included the ability to cause several [[Space Marines]] to explode with a single blast of [[psychic]] might. The Fiend could also hold hundreds of foes completely still, as he caused their bodies to tear apart. He nearly killed the [[Novamarines]]' entire [[Strike Force Ishmayn]] with this last ability, as he attacked the '''Mountain-plex Ajax'''. Only the sudden arrival of the Sisters of Silence', stopped this from occurring. Though the Fiend had been able to kill half of the Strike Force's members, before his death.{{Fn|1}}
*The '''Harvest''' - Dismembered a [[Warhound Titan]], during the fight for '''Hethker's Pass'''{{Fn|1}}
*The '''Headsman'''{{Fn|1}} 
*The '''Lament''' - Caused the death of an [[Orbital Defence Platform]]'s garrison, by whispering through a corrupted [[vox]] channel that could not be shut off.{{Fn|1}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[Codex: Adeptus Custodes (10th Edition)]], pgs. 30-33 - ''The Silent Sisterhood''

