Thucyid.wikitext:
{{DeathwatchPortal}}
{{ImperialFistsPortal}}
'''Thucyid''' is a [[Space Marine]] of the [[Deathwatch]], originally a [[Veteran Space Marine|Veteran]] of the [[Imperial Fists]] [[Chapter]].{{Fn|1}}

==Biography==
Thucyid was one of the Marines stationed at [[Watch Fortress]] [[Zarabek]] when it was discovered by the [[Ordo Xenos]] that [[human]] [[pirate]]s operating in the [[Teramus System]] somehow had access to functional [[Eldar]] [[lance]] weapons mounted on their ships. In a debate between the Marines present over the issue, [[Thucyid]] rebuked [[Gottrand]], who favoured a direct assault on the pirates to the point of accusing the other Marines of cowardice. Gottrand backed down from his argument, in part because, due to Thucyid's long years of service and use of heavy weapons, Gottrand equated him with one of his chapter's [[Long Fang]]s.{{Fn|1}}

In the end, [[Watch Captain]] [[Ska Mordentodt]] allowed [[Space Marine Sergeant|Sergeant]] [[Courlanth]] to assemble a [[Kill-Team]] to lead a mission into the Teramus system to uncover the source of the weapons and eliminate them; Thucyid was selected by Courlanth for the mission.{{Fn|1}}

Courlanth led the Kill-Team in infiltrating the pirates' [[Buketown|asteroid base]] and discovered that the pirate leader, [[Arlon Buke]], had entered into a pact with the [[Dark Eldar]] of the [[Kabal of the Crimson Blossom]]. When he saw that the pirates were trading captured slaves to the xenos in exchange for weapons and drugs, Courlanth abandoned stealth and ordered an attack on the Kabal and the pirates alike. Thucyid was injured by the Dark Eldars' [[Splinter Weaponry|splinter weapons]], but survived the battle.{{Fn|1}}

==Wargear==
Thucyid was armed with the [[heavy bolter]] ''[[Iolanth]]'', which was also chambered to accept [[Boltgun#Ammunition Types|special-issue ammunition]], including '''Inferno''' and '''Kraken''' rounds.{{Fn|1}}

