Titus Valens.wikitext:
{{SpaceMarinesPortal}}
{{otheruses|USE=White Consuls Chapter Master|OTHERUSE=[[Silver Templars]] [[Space Marine Dreadnought|Dreadnought]]|OTHERPAGE=Valens (Dreadnought)}}
'''Titus Valens''' was a [[Chapter Master]] of the [[White Consuls]], a [[Second Founding]] chapter derived from the [[Ultramarines]] [[geneseed]] and member of the [[Astartes Praeses]].

In a position unique to the White Consuls, he was actually one of two Masters that led the chapter in different aspects of the role: Titus was the battlemaster, excelling in leading his ground troops against the enemy, whereas [[Cymar Xydius]] is cunning and handles strategic command and planetary diplomacy.{{Fn|1}}

==History==
Titus fought valiantly during the [[Battle of the Boros Gate|Boros Gate campaign]].  Taking to the ground of [[Boros Prime]], the first planet in the system that the [[Word Bearers]] had set foot upon, Titus was instrumental in turning the tide of battle against the enemy.  He managed to stave off the majority of their attacks, relying on Coadjutator [[Gaius Aquilius]] to be the voice of the Imperial citizens of Boros Prime.  Unfortunately, Titus allowed himself to be overtaken by Chaos forces so that Aquilius along with a handful of White Consuls and Imperial Guard could escape.  He was killed in one-on-one combat with [[Burias Drak'Shal]], a possessed Chaos Marine Icon Bearer.{{Fn|2}}

