Tjaras Grunli.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Tjaras Grunli''' was a Legionary in the [[Space Wolves]] [[Space Marine Legion|Legion]], who took part in the [[Horus Heresy]]'s [[Siege of Terra]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
He was among the [[Imperials]], however, who were unable to retreat into the [[Sanctum Imperialis]], before it sealed its doors. This left Grunli and other such Imperials facing the overwhelming numbers of [[Warmaster]] [[Horus]]' [[Traitor]] forces. The [[Space Wolf]] would join with other [[Legionaries]] and [[Imperial Army]] survivors, though, and they fought the [[Death Guard]] in the [[Imperial Palace]]'s [[Irenic Barbican]]. In time, the Imperials were overwhelmed by the [[Traitor Legion]] and one by one Grunli's comrades met their end, until only he remained. The wrathful Space Wolf would reap a heavy toll amongst the Death Guard for this, however, until Grunli was mortally wounded by the Traitor [[Vorx]]. Instead of killing him, though, Vorx and the Death Guard moved on and left the dying Space Wolf for the [[Daemon]]s and [[Chaos Cultists|Cultist]] [[Haruspice]]s that followed them.{{Fn|1}} 

His possibly zombified corpse is later discovered by the [[White Scars]] after the battle.{{Fn|2}} 

==Sources==
*{{Endn|1}}: [[The End and the Death: Volume II (Novel)]], 5:xv
*{{Endn|2}}: [[The End and the Death: Volume III (Novel)]], Fragments (Agonal) - iii
