Tolbek Azhtar Sum.wikitext:
{{ThousandSonsPortal}}
'''Tolbek Azhtar Sum''' is a [[Thousand Sons]] [[Sorcerer]], who co-leads a [[Warpcoven]] that is among its forces that invaded [[Harlecrypt Tertius]], during the [[Prosperan Rift War]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
His [[Warpcoven]] is coated in [[Warp]]-tainted verdigris and are empyrically corroded. Their appearance led the [[Imperial]] on [[Harlecrypt Tertius]] to refer to Sum and his Warpcoven, as the '''Corroded Ghosts''' or the '''Rusted Covens'''. They appeared without warning and, though, they slew many of the Imperium's forces, Sum's Warcoven was focused on taking specific captives. According to information gathered by [[Interrogator]]-[[Lieutenant (Imperial Guard)|Lieutenant]] [[Idon Throom]], Sum's Warcoven was responsible for the kidnappings of [[Bishop (Ecclesiarchy)|Bishop]] [[Haraldus Threng]], [[Preceptoress]] [[Anjelis Gartayga]], [[Bombardier-General]] [[Azahel Blattnir]] and six other Imperial servants. All were important figures in the defense of Harlecrypt Tertius's '''Mausoleum City Seven''', but the Interrogator currently knows of little else that connects them together. However given the [[Thousand Sons]]' penchant for obscure schemes, he believes the Warpcoven undoubtedly had a reason to choose these individuals.{{Fn|1}} 
