Tolwyn Tan Draconis.wikitext:
{{ImperialKnightsPortal}}
'''{{PAGENAME}}''' was the [[High King]] of [[House Draconis]] and father of [[Jennika Tan Draconis]] and [[Danial Tan Draconis]].{{Fn|1}}{{Fn|3a}}{{Fn|3b}}

==Biography==
During the [[Ork Wars|First Ork War of Adrastapol]], Tolwyn served as '''Gatekeeper''' of his father's '''Exalted Court'''. He led a lance of twelve [[Knight]]s in the defence of House Draconis's keep [[Draconspire]] from the [[Ork]]s of [[Warboss]] [[Skarjaw]]. In the resulting battle, Skarjaw was beheaded by [[Markos Dar Draconis]] and the war was won shortly afterwards.{{Fn|2}} 

Tolwyn later became the [[High King]] of [[House Draconis]], and served in that role by the time that the [[Word Bearers]] [[Betrayal on Donatos|invaded]] the [[Imperium]] [[Industrial World]] [[Donatos]]; Tolwyn later led [[Adrastapol]]'s [[Knight House]]s to aid in its defence. However, disaster struck during the battle with the Word Bearers when the Adrastapolian Knight Houses, [[House Chimaeros|Chimaeros]] and [[House Wyvorn|Wyvorn]], began attacking their fellow Knights after their [[Throne Mechanicum|Thrones Mechanicum]] were tainted through [[Chaos]] witchery. In the bloody betrayal that followed, High King Tolwyn was killed and it fell to his son and heir, [[Danial Tan Draconis]], to rally together the remnants of Houses [[House Draconis|Draconis]], [[House Pegasson|Pegasson]] and [[House Minotos|Minotos]]' forces.{{Fn|1}}

==Knight Suit & Wargear==
In battle Tolwyn rode the [[Knight Paladin]] '''''[[Fyreheart]]''''', which was equipped with a relic laser-blade instead of the standard [[Reaper Chainsword]]. This blade, along with Tolwyn's crown, were claimed by the traitor '''Viscount''' [[Gerraint Tan Chimaeros]] after the High King's death.{{Fn|3b}}{{Fn|3c}}

