Torval Wyrdbane.wikitext:
{{SpaceWolvesPortal}}
'''Torval Wyrdbane, the Shadow Wolf,'''{{Fn|1c}} is the [[Wolf Lord]] of the [[Space Wolves]] [[Chapter]]'s [[Duskwolves]] [[Great Company]] and he wields the blade [[Vorskyr]].{{Fn|1b}}
==History==
Said to have earned and chosen his last name well, Wyrdbane is also known to be gifted with a [[Fenrisian Wolf|wolf]]'s low cunning. He was originally part of the [[Wolf Lord]] [[Vorek Gnarlfist]]'s [[Wolf Guard]], until Gnarlfist was killed in a battle with the [[Thousand Sons]] [[Traitor Legion]]. Wyrdbane was chosen as his successor and the new Wolf Lord pridefully chose{{Fn|1b}} the ill omened [[Spirit Wolf]] as a sigil,{{Fn|1a}} dismissing any curse or fate it was said to have. He then renamed the [[Iron Wolves]] as the [[Duskwolves]] and led them against the Thousand Sons to avenge Gnarlfist's death. They were victorious and in the battle's aftermath, the Wolf Lord began answering pleas of aid from [[Imperial]] worlds that were being invaded by the forces of [[Chaos]].{{Fn|1b}} This eventually led the Duskwolves to the blighted [[Stygius Sector]], which had largely fallen to a Chaos [[Invasion of the Stygius Sector|invasion]]. Wyrdbane now strikes at its fringes and provides hope to the outnumbered and cut off Imperial forces, that are still fighting within the Sector. Since his arrival, the Wolf Lord has taken the heads of at least four of the Thousand Sons' [[Sorcerers]], with the most notable being [[Kayesh Vrall]]. This occurred as the Duskwolves successfully purged the corrupted Stygius world, [[Kalimvar]].{{Fn|1c}} 

