Tray'ayr Cyberia.wikitext:
{{NecromundaPortal}}
'''Tray'ayr Cyberia''' was a powerful [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromundan]] gang leader, who sought to overthrow the [[Imperium]]'s rule of the [[Hive World]] in late [[M33]].{{Fn|1a}} 

==Biography==
At that time, [[Necromunda (planet)|Necromunda]] was wracked by instability as its rebellious population prevented the [[Hive World]] from providing its [[tithe]] of resources to the [[Imperium]].{{Fn|1b}} Cyberia was the only powerful gang leader at that time and sought to free the Hive World from the Imperium's rule and bring back the age of Necromunda's true rulers, the [[Iron Lords (Araneus Continuity)|Iron Lords]]. However, his rebellion was ended when Cyberia was killed by [[Martek Helm'ayr]]{{Fn|1a}} who was waging a war to bring order to Necromunda.{{Fn|1b}} Martek would succeed in his quest in and was rewarded by the Imperium by being made the Hive World's [[Planetary Governor]].{{Fn|1c}}

==Legacy==
Despite Cyberia's death, though, the gang leader's name would return to haunt Martek's descendants{{Fn|1d}} over the next two millennia.{{Fn|1e}} 

The first instance was in the [[Great Road War]] in 344.[[M34]], when a horde of [[Ash Waste nomad]]s, [[Mutants]] and [[Scavvies]] gathered under the command of a powerful wasteland warlord, who used them to attack the trade routes between Necromunda's [[Hive]]s. No one knew who the warlord was, but rumours abounded that he was a descendant of Cyberia, or perhaps even Cyberia himself, kept alive by [[Dark Age of Technology|Dark Age technology]]. While his hordes were finally broken by the ruling [[House Helm'ayr]]'s forces in 490.M34, there was no sign of what became of the warlord or who he truly was.{{Fn|1d}}

The ghost of Cyberia would strike at Martek's descendants a final time, when a mechanical creature known as the [[Cybernak]] surfaced in the depths of [[Hive Rothgol]] in 932.[[M35]]. Appearing to be a withered gang member, wearing a clicking spider-like helm, the Cybernak raised a rebel army within the Hive, while constantly whispering of an ancient war and [[Iron Lords (Araneus Continuity)|kings of iron]]. Its rebellion, though, was put down by Rothgol's [[Noble House|Noble]] and [[Clan House]]s, who captured the Cybernak and presented it as a gift to the current Lord [[House Helmawr|Helmawr]]. When the [[Planetary Governor]] met the mechanical creature, however, the Cybernak appeared to see Lord Helmawr as its ancient adversary, [[Martek Helm'ayr]].{{Fn|1e}}

