'''Tyborc''', also known as '''The Hero of Fort A-453''',{{Fn|3e}} was the [[Astra Militarum]] [[Colonel]] of the [[Death Korps of Krieg]]'s [[261st Krieg Siege Regiment]], when it took part in the [[Siege of Vraks]].{{Fn|1}}
==History==
{{Spoiler|source=Siege of Vraks (Novel)}}
===Fort A-453===
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"I had nightmarish visions of dying in my bed, an aged, feeble husk - and, for the first time, i am ashamed to say, I doubted that I was where the Emperor wanted me to be.<br>Could this truly have been His plan for me?"'''''
|source=''From the account of Veteran Colonel Tyborc.{{Fn|3f}}
|align=center
}}

Tyboc was the Captain of 9th Company{{Fn|3e}} of the 261st when he first deployed to Vraks between 812.[[M41]] and 815.[[M41]].{{Fn|3c}} Tyborc's first notable action in the [[Siege of Vraks|war]] was the capture of [[Fort A-453]]. Tyborc and the men under his command took the [[Vraksian Renegade Militia|traitor]] fort after a successful assault, and then managed to hold it for three days until being relieved.{{Fn|3d}} By the time reinforcements arrived, only eight of Tyborc’s men were still alive and Tyborc himself was injured.{{Fn|3g}} Tyborc was subsequently taken to a [[Officio Medicae|medicae]] facility to receive treatment. It was during this time that Tyborc first met [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus]]. [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] had dubbed Tyborc '''The Hero of Fort A-453'''{{Fn|3e}}, a title that Tyborc was uncomfortable with.{{Fn|2}} [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] tried to convince Tyborc that being a hero could inspire other Kriegsmen.{{Fn|3e}}

===Tyborc's Return to Service===
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"In some ways, Captain Tyborc, you and I are not so different. We desire, most of all, to make a difference. On occasion we have felt ourselves helpless to do so."'''''
|source=''[[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus]].{{Fn|3i}}
|align=center
}}
Tyborc was bedbound for some time, but eventually returned to limited duties. While behind the lines he sought out [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] again. During Tyborc’s absence, some of his men had been killed during an attack carried out by [[mutant]]s. Tyborc confided in [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] that he felt some frustration at not having died with his men due to his absence.{{Fn|3g}} 

When Tyborc returned to the trenches two weeks later, he found that his veteran [[Watchmaster]] had been replaced by a Watchmaster from the 3rd Company. Tyborc told his Watchmaster that he wished  he had been present during the [[mutant]] attack. The Watchmaster exclaimed that if 'The Hero of Fort A-453' had been present he could have saved many lives. Tyborc was repulsed by this, and stated he only wished he had been present so he could have died with his men.{{Fn|3g}} 

Tyborc begun to meet regulary with [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]]. Their talks begun to make him question his view on service to the Emperor. He begun to value his life, and saw that he could serve the Emperor by doing more than just dying.{{Fn|3h}} Over time [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] would become a confidant to Tyborc, and the two developed a deep trust.{{Fn|3i}}

Tyborc was shot and injured again during an offensive in 822.[[M41]].{{Fn|3j}}

===The Green Hell Offensive===
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"When gods and monsters clasehed above our heads, what did our efforts matter in the least?<br>What difference could our tiny, fragile lives possibly make - and who would even care to remember that we tried?."'''''
|source=''From the account of Veteran Colonel Tyborc.{{Fn|3k}}
|align=center
}}
On 509.826.[[M41]] Tyborc was promoted to Colonel of the [[261st Krieg Siege Regiment]], following the demise of his predecessor. The same year, [[Inquisitors]] of the [[Ordo Malleus]] were attached to each [[Death Korps]] [[regiment]] at [[Vraks]].{{Fn|3l}} Before the next large offensive, which was to be led by [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Thor Malkin]], Tyborc began to reflect that he no longer craved death as he once did. While far from a coward, he was now aware that he could serve the [[Emperor]] by living just as much as by dying.{{Fn|3m}} 

On the fifth day of the offensive, Tyborc's regiment marched into the '''Green Hell''', an area of [[Vraks]] overun by [[Death Guard]] [[Chaos Space Marines|Marines]] and the taint of [[Nurgle]]. Here he battled [[Plague Ogryn]]s and [[Plague Zombies|the dead of his own regiment]]. Tyborc killed the zombie that had previously been [[Colonel]] [[Keled]] of the [[19th Krieg Siege Regiment]].{{Fn|3n}} After this battle [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]] confirmed to Tyborc that [[daemons]] were present on [[Vraks]]. Tyborc had tried to speak to [[Colonel]] [[262 (Colonel)|262]], but the [[262nd Krieg Siege Regiment|262nd's]] [[Colonel]] was unwilling to speak of the [[daemons]] his unit had encountered.{{Fn|3o}} 

During this period [[daemons]] began to feature in Tyborc’s dreams. Prompted by [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus|Tenaxus]]'s words, Tyborc now beleived that he was a hero; that he could inspire his men and perhaps even be an heir to [[Colonel]] [[Jurten]].{{Fn|3o}}

===The Murder Slopes===
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"I first met Inquisitor Lord Rex when he sentenced me to death."'''''
|source=''From the account of Veteran Colonel Tyborc.{{Fn|3p}}
|align=center
}}
By the end of 829.[[M41]] [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Hector Rex]] could see the long [[Siege of Vraks|war's]] end was finally in sight. He met personally with Tyborc and charged him with leading the assault up the '''Murder Slopes''' to attack the '''Citadel Gate'''. Tyborc deeply respected [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Hector Rex|Rex]], and felt releived that he finally had a chance to die in battle, but to do so while making a difference.{{Fn|3q}}

The weeks leading up to the attack kept Tyborc busy. When the attack finally started, Tyborc was initially confined to the command bunker. He was desperate to lead the assault himself, as he had done at [[Fort A-453]]. The assault ground to a bloody halt as the [[Gorgon Armoured Assault Transport]]s of the [[261st Krieg Siege Regiment|261st]] were either destroyed or bogged down. As night fell Tyborc led the fourth, and final, wave of the assault on the Gate. He was accompanied by [[Leman Russ Battle Tank]]s, [[Atlas Recovery Vehicle]]s and [[Death Korps Grenadiers|Grenadiers]]. Tyborc took the banner of the [[261st Krieg Siege Regiment|261st]] with him up the 'Murder Slopes'.{{Fn|3q}} 

Tyborc fought against all manor of foes on the 'Murder Slopes', even managing to kill a [[Chaos Space Marine]]. However the success Tyborc had bought would soon be quickly reversed. Thunder and lightning filled the sky and soon [[daemons]] took to the field. The Krieg under his command begun to flee the field of battle, though those who could see the Hero of Fort A-453 stood their ground. Yet, as others began to retreat towards the [[269th Krieg Siege Regiment|269th]], Tyborc knew they would be fighting fellow Kriegsmen, and so, he gave the order to retreat. His [[commissar]] pulled his pistol, but found himself unable to execute Tyborc. The entire [[261st Krieg Siege Regiment|261st]] fled the battle, their banner being lost in the retreat.{{Fn|3q}} 

[[Colonel]] Tyborc was among the 261st's few survivors. His descion to order a retreat led to mercy being shown to the rank and file Korpsmen who fled the field,{{Fn|3q}}  but the 261st could no longer function as a Regiment. They were instead folded into the 30th Line Korps' three other Regiments (the [[262nd Krieg Siege Regiment|262nd]], [[263rd Krieg Siege Regiment|263rd]], and [[269th Krieg Siege Regiment|269th]]),{{Fn|1}} while Colonel Tyborc was taken into [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Hector Rex|Rex]]'s custody.{{Fn|3s}}

===Inquisitorial Service===
{{QuoteBox
|quote = '''''"I can see how the stories told to the Krieg, my people, condition us to think ourselves unworthy, to see ourselves as somehow less than human. I also see why this is wholly necessary, for how else could we accept our appointed role...<br>How else could we ever find redemption?"'''''
|source=''From the account of Veteran Colonel Tyborc.{{Fn|3r}}
|align=center
}}
Tyborc's retreat had destroyed his image as a hero among the Krieg; even those who didn't know what had happened now refused to speak of Tyborc.{{Fn|3u}} Tyborc spent weeks confined to quarters, where his only visitor was [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Thor Malkin]]. Tyborc was confused to find that [[Thor Malkin]] was understanding of Tyborc's descions on the 'Murder Slopes'.  Tyborc expressed a desire to speak with [[Confessor]] [[Agnae Tenaxus]], but was told she was unavaliable.{{Fn|3w}} In reality she was dead.{{Fn|3t}} 

Another week passed before Tyborc was brought a fresh uniform and summoned by [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Hector Rex|Rex]].{{Fn|3w}} Tyborc had been promoted to the General Staff.{{Fn|1}} He felt this must have an administrative error.{{Fn|3w}} But Tyborc would once more take to the field of battle. Some among the Krieg saw him once again as a hero.{{Fn|3v}} However, this opinion was not shared by Krieg High Command, who still wished him executed for cowardice. [[Inquisitor Lord]] [[Hector Rex|Rex]] felt that Tyborc would be far more useful on his staff and so permanently seconded Tyborc to the [[Ordo Malleus]].{{Fn|3w}}

